"mt_okUMpHsV-P":{"intro":"Let's explore neurons and the brain! 🧠⚡","items":[{"t":"order","q":"Put a nerve signal's path in order.","steps":["Dendrites receive a signal","Impulse travels along the axon","Chemicals cross the synapse","Next neuron is activated"]},{"t":"match","q":"Match each brain area to a function.","pairs":[["frontal lobe","planning and decisions"],["occipital lobe","vision"],["temporal lobe","hearing and memory"],["limbic system","emotions"]]},{"t":"pick","q":"What is neuroplasticity?","opts":["The brain changing as you learn and practice","Brains made of plastic","The brain stopping growth at 5"],"why":"Practice strengthens connections."},{"t":"tf","q":"Signals cross a synapse using chemicals called neurotransmitters.","a":true,"why":"That's the chemical part of electrochemical."},{"t":"pick","q":"Which part coordinates balance and smooth movement?","opts":["Cerebellum","Occipital lobe","Spinal fluid"],"why":"The cerebellum fine-tunes movement."}]},
"mt_0sELh0MYWb":{"intro":"Let's unzip the code of life — DNA! 🧬","items":[{"t":"match","q":"Match each DNA base to its partner.","pairs":[["A (adenine)","T (thymine)"],["C (cytosine)","G (guanine)"],["T (thymine)","A (adenine)"]]},{"t":"pick","q":"What shape is DNA?","opts":["Double helix","Single circle","Flat square"],"why":"Two twisted strands like a spiral ladder."},{"t":"order","q":"Put the central dogma in order.","steps":["DNA","mRNA","Protein"]},{"t":"pick","q":"A gene is…","opts":["a section of DNA that codes for a protein","a whole cell","a type of sugar"],"why":"Genes are instructions for making proteins."},{"t":"tf","q":"Gene editing raises ethical questions about safety and fairness.","a":true,"why":"Scientists and society debate how to use it responsibly."}]},
"mt_J40cOn7VWn":{"intro":"Your body is always balancing itself! ⚖️🌡️","items":[{"t":"pick","q":"What is homeostasis?","opts":["Keeping a stable internal environment","Growing taller","Digesting food"],"why":"The body keeps temperature, sugar and water steady."},{"t":"match","q":"Match each hormone or response to its effect.","pairs":[["insulin","lowers blood glucose"],["glucagon","raises blood glucose"],["sweating","cools the body"],["shivering","warms the body"]]},{"t":"order","q":"Put this negative feedback loop in order.","steps":["Blood glucose rises after a meal","Pancreas detects the rise","Pancreas releases insulin","Cells take in glucose","Blood glucose returns to normal"]},{"t":"tf","q":"Negative feedback reverses a change to bring things back to normal.","a":true,"why":"It counteracts the change."},{"t":"pick","q":"In type 1 diabetes, the body cannot make enough…","opts":["insulin","oxygen","calcium"],"why":"So blood glucose can't be controlled without treatment."}]},
"mt_roinupb_7L":{"intro":"Let's explore how cells can go wrong — and help heal! 🔬","items":[{"t":"pick","q":"What causes cancer?","opts":["DNA mutations that break cell-division controls","Eating one candy","Catching a cold"],"why":"Cells then divide uncontrollably."},{"t":"pick","q":"A mass of cells dividing out of control is called a…","opts":["tumor","tissue graft","vaccine"],"why":"Tumors can be benign or malignant."},{"t":"sort","q":"Stem cell or specialized cell?","bins":["Stem cell","Specialized cell"],"items":[["can become many cell types",0],["red blood cell",1],["nerve cell",1],["found in bone marrow and embryos",0]],"why":"Stem cells haven't yet specialized."},{"t":"tf","q":"Stem cells could be used to repair damaged tissues.","a":true,"why":"That's the goal of regenerative medicine."},{"t":"pick","q":"Which choice lowers the risk of some cancers?","opts":["Not smoking and wearing sunscreen","Using tanning beds","Smoking"],"why":"Avoiding carcinogens reduces mutations."}]},
