"mt_NVr4AhsvIq":{"intro":"Why does the ground shake? Let's find out! 💥","items":[{"t":"pick","q":"What causes an earthquake?","opts":["Rocks underground suddenly slip or break","Thunder","Heavy traffic"],"why":"Built-up stress is suddenly released."},{"t":"order","q":"Put these steps in order.","steps":["Rocks push against each other","Stress builds up","Rocks suddenly slip","Energy shakes the ground"]},{"t":"pick","q":"A crack where rocks move past each other is called a…","opts":["fault","crater","vent"],"why":"Earthquakes happen along faults."},{"t":"tf","q":"An earthquake releases energy that travels through the ground.","a":true,"why":"These are called seismic waves."},{"t":"pick","q":"Bend a stick until it snaps. That snap is like…","opts":["rocks breaking in an earthquake","a volcano erupting","a river flowing"],"why":"Stress builds then suddenly releases."}]},
