"mt_rML9unnd9x":{"intro":"Famous eruptions and moving continents! 🌋🌍","items":[{"t":"match","q":"Match each eruption to a fact.","pairs":[["Mount St. Helens 1980","erupted in Washington State"],["Eyjafjallajökull 2010","ash cloud grounded flights over Europe"],["Tambora 1815","led to the 'Year Without a Summer'"]]},{"t":"pick","q":"How can huge eruptions cool the planet?","opts":["Ash and gases block sunlight","They add more sunshine","They melt the poles"],"why":"Particles high in the air reflect sunlight."},{"t":"pick","q":"What was Pangaea?","opts":["A supercontinent of joined landmasses","A volcano","An ocean"],"why":"About 300 to 200 million years ago, the continents were joined."},{"t":"tf","q":"Continents still move a few centimeters each year.","a":true,"why":"About as fast as your fingernails grow."},{"t":"pick","q":"Which clue suggests continents were once joined?","opts":["South America and Africa fit like puzzle pieces","All continents are green","Oceans are salty"],"why":"Matching coastlines and fossils support it."}]},
